{
  "mn136:0.1": "Middle Discourses 136 ",
  "mn136:0.2": "The Longer Analysis of Deeds ",
  "mn136:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "mn136:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha in the Bamboo Grove, the squirrels’ feeding ground. ",
  "mn136:2.1": "Now at that time Venerable Samiddhi was staying in a wilderness hut. ",
  "mn136:2.2": "Then as the wanderer Potaliputta was going for a walk he came up to Venerable Samiddhi and exchanged greetings with him. ",
  "mn136:2.3": "When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to him: ",
  "mn136:2.4": "“Reverend Samiddhi, I have heard and learned this in the presence of the ascetic Gotama: ",
  "mn136:2.5": "‘Deeds by way of body and speech are done in vain. Only mental deeds are real.’ ",
  "mn136:2.6": "And: ‘There is such an attainment where the one who enters it does not feel anything at all.’” ",
  "mn136:2.7": "“Don’t say that, Reverend Potaliputta, don’t say that! Don’t misrepresent the Buddha, for misrepresentation of the Buddha is not good. And the Buddha would not say this: ",
  "mn136:2.8": "‘Deeds by way of body and speech are done in vain. Only mental deeds are real.’ ",
  "mn136:2.9": "But, reverend, there is such an attainment where the one who enters it does not feel anything at all.” ",
  "mn136:2.10": "“Reverend Samiddhi, how long has it been since you went forth?” ",
  "mn136:2.11": "“Not long, reverend: three years.” ",
